In article <ghartzogCptE50.FD2@netcom.com>, ghartzog@netcom.com (Greg Hartzog) 
writes:

>I got the source code from gatekeeper.dec.com and seems to be fine.  In 
>building BISON I have two problems.  First, I can not get the macro assembler
>to work on the file VMSHLP.MAC.  I have tried both MACRO and 
>MACRO/MIGRATION/ENABLE=GLOBAL.  Neither will build the VMSHLP file without
>errors.  (VMSHLP has ALLOCA and BCOPY assembler source in it).  

Note that DEC C for OpenVMS AXP has alloca() as a builtin function, so
you don't need the macro version.  Also, it would be simpler to define
a macro for bcopy something like:

  #define bcopy(src,dest,len)  memcpy(dest,src,len)

If you include string.h, then the builtin function form of memcpy can also
be used.

>Also, the linker can not find the symbol _IOTABLE anywhere in its stuff.  I 
>have included VAXCRTL in the link options with no success.  Does anyone know
>what the routine _IOTABLE does and where it lives?

I'm not familiar with _IOTABLE, but you shouldn't be including VAXCRTL in
your link on an AXP system.  There, you should be using the DEC C RTL,
which is in STARLET and is automatically searched by the linker.

